sec.p:
Based on the functional community labels, we further proposed a metric called binding breadth index (BBI) to quantify the potential olfactory breadth of a group of ORs toward a particular class of VOCs. To correct for sampling bias caused by small community sizes, we applied the Wilson score interval.
Wilsonscore(Wk)=pk+z22n−zpk(1−pk)n+z24n21+z2n \begin{document}$$\displaystyle Wilson \, score \, \left(W_{k}\right)=\frac{p_{k}+\frac{z^{2}}{2 n}-z \sqrt{\frac{p_{k}\left(1-p_{k}\right)}{n}+\frac{z^{2}}{4 n^{2}}}}{1+\frac{z^{2}}{n}}$$\end{document}
The definitions are as follows: (1) n: total number of ORs in the community; (2) pk: proportion of ORs in the kth community; (3) z: Z-score for the 95% confidence level (z = 1.96)

The BBI for the ith functional group of VOCs is defined as:
BBIi=∑k=1n(Wk⋅Fki) \begin{document}$$\displaystyle B B I_{i}=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\left(W_{k} \cdot F_{k i}\right)$$\end{document}
Where: (1) Wk: Wilson score for the kth community; (2) Fki: the functional label matrix element representing the recognition score of kth community for ith functional group of VOCs; (3) n: the total number of docking-derived functional communities (n=6)
